From 53adadec10288c8b1ce81547b7fd38090b99595a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rogerbacardit <rogerbacardit@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 23:12:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] Twister: a continuous parameter follows the ring's
 position, full range

Two faults kept a Twister knob from reaching a parameter's ends:

- Each relative step moved range/200 (Schwung's knob_engine), so the 128
  steps of a factory Twister's travel crossed only 64 % of the range. A
  continuous parameter with a min/max is now set from the ring's position
  (ext-param-steps continuousAt), linear like Schwung's normalizedOf, so the
  ring the follow puts back is exactly where the turn continues.
- The ring resync ran only on a rendered frame; an idle page renders none
  once the turn stops, so the ring was left at its end. twisterFollowRest
  replays the last levels from the tick once a hold expires.

Tier: local suites (abi-parity skipped: needs the author's schwung path, red
on main too) + deployed and tried by hand on the device; device tier not run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
